+## Failure path
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` takes the same failure path as any other turn failure: `onError` fires with the session and the thrown error, `afterSession` fires after it, and the rejection still reaches the caller, while none of the later hooks runs, the provider is not called and no entry is added to the session. `afterSession` therefore also runs for a turn that never started: it cannot assume any hook after `beforeSession` ran, and a deployer who allocates in `beforeSession` and releases in `afterSession` releases an allocation the turn never used ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws and still rejects the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
